Widen the Tcl-side key-length locals to Tcl_Size for Tcl 9.

Tcl_GetByteArrayFromObj's third parameter widened from int* to Tcl_Size*
(a long) in Tcl 9, to support byte arrays bigger than INT_MAX. SQLCipher's
key/rekey/open -key handling in tclsqlite.c still declares nKey as a plain
int, which is now an incompatible-pointer-type compile error against Tcl 9
headers. Widen the two declarations; nKey still narrows back to int at the
sqlite3_key/sqlite3_rekey call sites (both take a plain int length), which
is fine since a passphrase is always tiny.

diff --git a/src/tclsqlite.c b/src/tclsqlite.c
index 65c95db..7436dfd 100644
--- a/src/tclsqlite.c
+++ b/src/tclsqlite.c
@@ -3659,7 +3659,7 @@ deserialize_error:
   case DB_REKEY: {
 /* BEGIN SQLCIPHER */
 #if defined(SQLITE_HAS_CODEC) && !defined(SQLITE_OMIT_CODEC_FROM_TCL)
-    int nKey;
+    Tcl_Size nKey;
     void *pKey;
 #endif
 /* END SQLCIPHER */
@@ -4289,7 +4289,7 @@ static int SQLITE_TCLAPI DbMain(
 /* BEGIN SQLCIPHER */
 #if defined(SQLITE_HAS_CODEC) && !defined(SQLITE_OMIT_CODEC_FROM_TCL)
   void *pKey = 0;
-  int nKey = 0;
+  Tcl_Size nKey = 0;
 #endif
 /* END SQLCIPHER */
   int rc;
